---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.ts';
---

<Layout title="Privacy policy" description={`How ${site.name} handles subtitle files, analytics, cookies, and contact data.`}>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <h2>Your files</h2>
    <p>Every tool runs in your browser. Files are read and changed on your device. They are never uploaded to us, and we cannot see their names, contents, or subtitle text.</p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>If you accept, Google Analytics 4 records page views and tool use. Tool events include the tool name and file format, such as "SRT to WebVTT". They never include file names, file content, or subtitle text.</p>
    <p>If you reject, or have not chosen yet, analytics stays off. Consent Mode keeps analytics storage denied until you accept.</p>
    <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <p>Google Analytics sets cookies (named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>) only after you accept. We save your accept or reject choice in your browser's local storage, so we don't ask again.</p>
    <p>You can change your choice at any time: <button type="button" class="change" data-consent-open>change cookie settings</button>. The footer has the same link.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .change { background: none; border: 0; padding: 0; font: inherit; color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; cursor: pointer; }
</style>
